type FloorBatchStopPolicy = StopBeforeDependents | FullLedger

type RuntimeUnitCount = RuntimeUnitCountObserved { units: Nat } | RuntimeUnitCountUnavailable { cause: String }

data gunbc_ci_floor_batch_runtime_unit_count_note: String = "RUNTIME UNIT COUNT for the derived batch clamp (gunbc_ci_floor_batch_clamp_note): claim_executor alone knows the affected-set-selected unit count at enforcement time. RuntimeUnitCountObserved carries the count used in clamp_ms = overhead_seconds*1000 + units * per_unit_ms. RuntimeUnitCountUnavailable means the count was lost — typically a hard discovery error discarded DiscoverySummary at the Result boundary so corpus_witnesses reads 0 while the batch is a discovery aggregate, not a single-claim gate row. When unavailable the clamp comparison is REFUSED (verdict ClampRefused): a third state, not WithinBudget and not OverBudget — never map zero to one and render a corpus failure as FLOOR-BATCH-OVER-BUDGET. Authority type here; observation and enforcement live in claim_executor.rs (see gunbc_ci_floor_batch_runtime_unit_count_claim_executor_seed_note)."

data gunbc_ci_floor_batch_runtime_unit_count_claim_executor_seed_note: String = "§7 seed-retained HAND-RUST bridge (src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_executor.rs): FloorRuntimeUnitCount enum mirrors RuntimeUnitCount; each ClaimResult carries the observation; batch aggregation refuses the clamp when any row is Unavailable. Reason: unit-count availability is executor realization over batch results, not yet expressible as substrate behavior inside claim_executor. Dissolve-on: v2 self-emitted claim_executor when the executor bin crosses the self-host frontier."

data gunbc_ci_floor_batch_runtime_unit_count_claim_executor_seed_disposition: Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "gunbc.ci_spec",
    decl_name: "RuntimeUnitCount",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}

data gunbc_ci_ordinary_floor_budget_minutes: Minute = minute(count: 80)

data gunbc_ci_admission_postcondition_budget_minutes: Minute = minute(count: 5)

data gunbc_ci_walk_overhead_allowance_minutes: Minute = minute(count: 15)

fn gunbc_ci_workflow_wrapper_budget_minutes() -> Minute {
  minute(count: minute_count(m: gunbc_ci_ordinary_floor_budget_minutes) + minute_count(m: gunbc_ci_admission_postcondition_budget_minutes) + minute_count(m: gunbc_ci_walk_overhead_allowance_minutes))
}

data gunbc_ci_two_population_budget_note: String = "The CI walk owns two disjoint wall allowances: 55 minutes for ordinary batches and 5 minutes for green-only admission postconditions. WalkPlan carries both so claim_executor, not the outer runner, prevents ordinary work from consuming the admission allowance. The wall spent OUTSIDE both populations — the pre-walk capture subprocess, plan resolve, finalization and receipt writes, phase-journal flushes — is neither ordinary nor postcondition work, so the GitHub step wrapper reserves the named gunbc_ci_walk_overhead_allowance_minutes term for it rather than silently letting a slow pre-walk eat the ordinary allowance from the outside (review 47517; the two watchdogs bound their own populations, and the wrapper is strictly the three-term sum, 75 minutes today). A budget refusal is located to its population inside the executor; a wrapper kill with both populations under budget is located to the overhead term. The overhead term was raised 5→15 minutes (2026-08-05): measured CI floor pre-walk plus eager compile-clean install routinely exceeds 10 minutes before the ordinary population clock starts, so a 5-minute allowance let the GitHub step wrapper kill the job while ordinary budget remained — silent wrapper kill, not ordinary exhaustion. OPERATOR-SIGNED RAISE (briansrls, 2026-08-11): ordinary floor 55 -> 80 minutes, +45.5 percent; the wrapper sum follows derivedly, 75 -> 100. RUN ID: 31467399193 job 93706807817 @ cdabd41 on PR #8091, ORDINARY-FLOOR-OVER-BUDGET at population_index=4 (discovery batch), elapsed_ms=3300000 == budget_ms=3300000. THE ENROLLMENT THAT GREW THE BATCH: none, and as with all three batch-3 raises before it that mismatch with the template IS the receipt - the ordinary floor is affected-set-denominated, and this diff touches std.measure and std.induction and adds a std module beneath both, so the import closure selected 892 of 1074 entry groups (0.83) and discovered 8681 witnesses. SIZING, and its honesty class: 55 minutes is a CENSORED LOWER BOUND, not a measurement - the walk was refused while still running, so the true demand was never observed and cannot be quoted. The number is therefore an EXTRAPOLATION: 3300s at 892/1074 groups extrapolates linearly to ~3973s (66.2min) for the full selection, times the 1.2 measured fleet spread this family already funds elsewhere (the batch-4 raise cites 7.5-20 percent across srv2-02/srv3-01 on identical content) = ~4768s, rounded to 80 at whole-minute grain. THE ASSUMPTION THAT COULD BE WRONG: per-group cost is taken as uniform across the 182 unexecuted groups; if the tail is dearer than the head, 80 still reds and the remedy stays diagnose-or-signed-raise. WHAT THE RUN ACTUALLY SPENT IT ON, because the raise should not be mistaken for the fix: eval - running witnesses - was 122s, 3.7 percent of the budget. resolve was 2070s, and inside the assembly split rewire_import_str ALONE was 1189s, 36 percent of the entire ordinary allowance, with services 212s, symbol_index 192s and emit_info 181s behind it. This raise buys time for a cost shape that belongs to the per-entry assembly decomposition lane (#7597) and the five-minute-CI-gate program; it does not improve it, and it should TIGHTEN by ordinary receipt note when that lane lands. A SECOND FINDING, independent of this PR and larger than it: gunbc_ci_floor_batch_clamp_note sizes the discovery clamp against \"a full corpus of ~2316 witnesses clamps at ~44min\". This run discovered 8681. The clamp's stated sizing basis is ~3.7x stale against the corpus it governs, so a deep-std diff is simply the first shape to walk into a wall every broad diff now approaches; re-denominating that basis is owed and is not done here."

data gunbc_ci_floor_batch_stop_policy_note: String = "Floor batch stop policy (operator ruling 2026-07-22, fail-fast lane): claim_executor's walk halt is event-scoped so cheap-gate-early reorder does not truncate main's ledger. pull_request → StopBeforeDependents (fail-fast: a cheap-gate red stops before compile/corpus). push (main) and schedule (falsifier) → FullLedger (record batch failure and continue; exit non-zero at end). Unknown/unrecognized events default to FullLedger — never silently stop-early and lose ledger (the absorbing fallback). Authority: gunbc_ci_floor_batch_stop_policy_for_github_event in v2.workflow.ci_floor_plan; consumer: claim_executor.rs run_walk (see gunbc_ci_floor_batch_stop_policy_claim_executor_seed_note)."

data gunbc_ci_floor_batch_stop_policy_claim_executor_seed_note: String = "§7 seed-retained HAND-RUST bridge (src/v1/stage0/src/bin/claim_executor.rs): FloorBatchStopPolicy enum mirrors this type; run_walk halts or continues based on the variant returned by gunbc_ci_floor_batch_stop_policy_for_github_event after gunbc_ci_floor_plan_uses_batch_stop_policy gates enrollment. Reason: batch-walk halt is executor realization — host-process control flow over an already-evaluated .dag policy, not yet expressible as substrate behavior inside claim_executor. Checkable receipts: witness_floor_stop_policy_* + witness_floor_batch_stop_policy_plan_roster_enrolled in ci_floor_plan_witness_test; acceptance measurement (PR fail-fast ~2min; main push prints complete gate+corpus ledger under FullLedger). Dissolve-on: v2 self-emitted claim_executor run_walk when the executor bin crosses the self-host frontier (DESIGN §7 terminal collapse of stage0 host bins)."

data gunbc_ci_floor_batch_stop_policy_claim_executor_seed_disposition: Disposition = Scaffold {
  dissolves_to: SingleAuthority,
  bind: DeclarationRef {
    module_path: "gunbc.ci_spec",
    decl_name: "FloorBatchStopPolicy",
    field: WholeDeclaration
  }
}

