// THE UNGATED FLEET-DESIRED ADVANCE WAS DELETED HERE, and the deletion is the point rather than a
// tidy-up. What stood here was gunbc_ci_advance_fleet_desired_script, a concat-built shell step
// that pushed $GITHUB_SHA onto refs/fleet/desired -- with a compare-and-swap on the observed prior
// on the advance branch, and on the CREATE branch a bare `git push origin "$GITHUB_SHA:$DESIRED_REF"`
// carrying no lease at all, which is the branch that runs when the ref does not yet exist.
//
// The CAS half was correct. The ADMISSION half did not exist: gunbc.fleet_main_revision requires the
// desired revision to derive from merged, FLOOR-GREEN main and models that gate as
// decide_fleet_desired_advance, and this script never called it -- so the gate's only caller was its
// own witness test while the unproven path ran on every push to main. That is exactly the raw-HEAD
// advance the authority names as its prevented class, and it reached further than the ref:
// gunbc.roadmap_belt_actuate gates worker dispatch on revision standing, so a desired ref equal to
// whatever last landed made that gate agree unconditionally and pass in silence.
//
// The replacement is gunbc.fleet_desired_admission, whose decision consults the modeled gate with a
// floor conclusion observed from the floor run's own workflow_run payload, and which renders the
// authorized push itself so the surrounding shell carries no ref, revision or prior of its own. It
// is cut at the root rather than kept beside the replacement: two answers to how the fleet's
// admitted revision advances is the fork DESIGN section 3 forbids, and the weaker one was the live
// one. Keeping a function that can still render the raw form would leave the unsafe spelling one
// call site from returning. The script's only other consumers were gunbc.live_deploy_workflow and
// its witness file, both deleted with the deploy workflow authority.
//
// The Scaffold disposition and dissolution trigger that tracked this script's medium-as-string debt
// went with it -- the replacement's actuation is a model-rendered script, so that debt is re-declared
// where the remaining shell actually lives, not inherited here.
//
// This annotation was itself a merge conflict: the root cut and the admission change each deleted
// this script and each wrote their own account of why. Two annotations for one deletion is the
// duplication section 3 forbids, so they are merged here rather than stacked, and the accompanying
// `data ..._deleted_note: String` row is dropped -- a String declaration whose sole purpose is
// commentary is the misplaced data section 4c names, and the annotation above already carries it.




